# Campus Clinic Management System

## About the Project

The Campus Clinic Management System is a role-based appointment management system built with FastAPI, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It allows students to book appointments with doctors while enabling doctors to manage and update appointment statuses in real time.

I initially built this project as a backend-focused application because I am currently learning Backend Development. However, after taking an interview test that involved frontend concepts, I was inspired to challenge myself by adding a user interface to one of my projects. This gave me the opportunity to explore how the frontend communicates with APIs and provided valuable experience working across both the backend and frontend of an application.

This project became more than just an appointment system—it became a practical way for me to learn authentication, role-based access control, API integration, and full-stack development concepts.

## Features

* User Registration and Login
* JWT Authentication and Authorization
* Role-Based Access Control (Student and Doctor)
* Book Appointments
* View Appointments
* Update Appointment Status (Pending, Confirmed, Cancelled)
* Protected Dashboard Routes
* Pagination Support
* Appointment Filtering
* Responsive User Interface
* Logout Functionality
* Loading and Error Handling Messages

## Technologies Used

### Backend

* Python
* FastAPI
* SQLAlchemy
* SQLite
* JWT Authentication

### Frontend

* HTML
* CSS
* JavaScript

## User Roles

### Student

Students can:

* Register and Login
* Book appointments with doctors
* View appointment statuses
* Logout securely

### Doctor

Doctors can:

* Login to their dashboard
* View appointments assigned to them
* Confirm appointments
* Cancel appointments
* Logout securely

## Appointment Workflow

```text
Student Books Appointment
            ↓
         Pending
            ↓
Doctor Reviews Appointment
       ↙            ↘
 Confirmed         Cancelled
            ↓
Student Receives Updated Status
```

